lor=\"#ff0000\">In addition: Warning message:</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">In one_of(c(&quot;GEO.id&quot;, &quot;GEO.id2&quot;, &quot;<a href=\"http://GEO.annotation.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://GEO.annotation.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467203604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oIq9G3lqUUqF5uBcLiNL_\">GEO.annotation.id</a>&quot;, &quot;NAICS.id&quot;,  :</font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">  Unknown variables: `GEO.id`, `GEO.id2`, `<a href=\"http://GEO.annotation.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://GEO.annotation.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467203604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oIq9G3lqUUqF5uBcLiNL_\">GEO.annotation.id</a>`, `NAICS.id`, `<a href=\"http://NAICS.annotation.id\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://NAICS.annotation.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467203604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1aXjGhbUJbVFPh2hW_IMf4\">NAICS.annotation.id</a>`, `CBOGROUP.id`, `CBOSEX.id`, `YEAR.id`</font></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I also tried the base aggregate function</div><div>data_aggregated &lt;- aggregate( df[ dataVars], by=as.list( data_subset[ idVars ] ), sum )</div><div><br></div><div>This gives me an empty data frame. </div><div><br></div><div>I will greatly appreciate any ideas. </div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
